    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0381" n="373" xml:id="pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.9131/145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversation, by Mr. Cecil T.
                        White of the Division of Commercial Policy and Agreements</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-10">May 10, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister<anchor n="40" xml:id="d346-f1"/> telephoned to inquire whether we
                    could give him our answer to the Iranian draft proposal of September 3,
                    1940.</p>
                <p>I replied in the negative, but informed the Minister that the basic studies now
                    have been completed and I thought it likely that our reply would be ready within
                    the next two weeks.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d346-f1" n="40" xml:id="d346-f1-content">
                <p>Iranian Minister Mohammed Schayesteh.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
